# Sobelow skips for the two findings that have no function or pipeline to
# carry a `# sobelow_skip` annotation (sobelow 0.16, #1006). sobelow builds a
# fingerprint from the finding's type, file and line alone, so neither entry
# comes back when its site changes in place: each waives its check at that
# site, and a test pins what the waiver relies on instead.
# test/portfolixir/ci_test.exs holds this file to exactly these two lines.
#
# Config.HTTPS (config/prod.exs): TLS is terminated by the operator's reverse
# proxy (ADR-0045 2), and PHX_FORCE_SSL is the runtime opt-in that redirects
# and sets HSTS (PortfolixirWeb.OptionalSsl; D-2 of the Sprint 11 plan, #382).
# sobelow 0.16 clears the check only for TLS forced in prod.exs, so this entry
# waives it for good: its fingerprint names line 0 and never changes. The
# posture is pinned by ci_test.exs ("prod.exs states the HTTPS posture") and
# session_hardening_test.exs (the PHX_FORCE_SSL opt-in).
#
# Config.CSWH (lib/portfolixir_web/endpoint.ex): the LiveView socket inherits
# the endpoint's check_origin, which config/runtime.exs sets in a release to
# the Host guard's allow-list (PHX_HOST, loopback and PORTFOLIXIR_ALLOWED_HOSTS,
# #758). sobelow cannot read a list built at runtime and reports it at low
# confidence. An override on the socket line would keep this fingerprint, so
# live_socket_origin_test.exs pins the behaviour: a foreign Origin is refused,
# and a release's check_origin is the allow-list.
